00:18:00,689 --> 00:18:02,689
Yo-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

259
00:18:04,089 --> 00:18:06,769
Yo-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

260
00:18:08,109 --> 00:18:11,109
Yo-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

261
00:18:11,109 --> 00:18:12,249
Yo-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

262
00:18:12,249 --> 00:18:14,409
Gather up all of the crew!

263
00:18:14,549 --> 00:18:16,549
It's time to ship out Binx's crew!

264
00:18:16,769 --> 00:18:18,729
Sea wind blows to where who knows?

265
00:18:18,789 --> 00:18:20,649
The waves will be our guide!

266
00:18:20,649 --> 00:18:25,229
Or across the ocean's tide, rays of sunshine far and wide

267
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:29,429
Birds they sing of cheerful things in circles passing by

268
00:18:29,429 --> 00:18:33,669
Bid farewell to Weaverstown, say so long to Port Renown

269
00:18:33,669 --> 00:18:37,909
Sing a song, it won't be long before we're casting off

270
00:18:37,909 --> 00:18:42,269
Across the gold and silver seas, a salty spray puts us at ease

271
00:18:42,269 --> 00:18:46,469
Day and night to our delight, the voyage never ends

272
00:18:46,469 --> 00:18:50,829
Gather up all of the crew, it's time to ship out Binx's crew

273
00:18:50,829 --> 00:18:54,949
Pirates, we eternally are challenging the sea

274
00:18:54,949 --> 00:18:59,429
With the waves to rest our heads, ship beneath us as our beds

275
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:03,689
Hoisted high upon the mast, our Jolly Roger flies

276
00:19:03,689 --> 00:19:08,009
Somewhere in the endless sky, stormy winds are blowing by

277
00:19:08,009 --> 00:19:11,349
Waves are dancing, even comes it's time to sound the drums

278
00:19:11,349 --> 00:19:13,529
How about that? They're heading upward too

279
00:19:13,529 --> 00:19:16,529
Now this is what I call traveling in style

280
00:19:16,529 --> 00:19:20,749
So pound your feet and clap your hands till Sunday's return

281
00:19:20,749 --> 00:19:38,529
Yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho, yo-ho-ho-ho

282
00:19:43,529 --> 00:19:47,449
Here comes the new world, the final sea on the Grand Line

283
00:19:47,449 --> 00:19:49,529
We're almost there, guys

284
00:19:49,529 --> 00:19:51,129
Sure took long enough

285
00:19:51,129 --> 00:19:54,129
Uh, Luffy?

286
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:57,289
Hey!

287
00:20:04,989 --> 00:20:05,989
That's it!

288
00:20:06,809 --> 00:20:08,449
We've come so far

289
00:20:08,449 --> 00:20:15,449
We're just there

290
00:20:15,449 --> 00:20:16,449
But all of you

291
00:20:16,749 --> 00:20:17,689
I want to give this

292
00:20:17,689 --> 00:20:20,829
I want to give this

293
00:20:23,469 --> 00:20:25,429
I want to give this

294
00:20:25,429 --> 00:20:26,369
Welcome

295
00:20:26,369 --> 00:20:28,249
I want to give this

296
00:20:28,249 --> 00:20:29,389
To me

297
00:20:29,389 --> 00:20:30,089
I want to give this

298
00:20:30,089 --> 00:20:30,969
I want to give this

299
00:20:30,969 --> 00:20:31,369
On the contrary

300
00:20:31,369 --> 00:20:32,249
Notice

301
00:20:32,249 --> 00:20:33,309
everyone

302
00:20:33,309 --> 00:20:34,249
I want to give this

303
00:20:34,249 --> 00:20:35,669
Take 30 cent

304
00:20:35,669 --> 00:20:36,769
I want to give this

305
00:20:36,769 --> 00:21:06,749
Thank you.

306
00:21:06,769 --> 00:21:23,309
Ready, crew? Count down with me!

307
00:21:23,309 --> 00:21:33,389
Ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three, two, one!

308
00:21:36,769 --> 00:21:43,169
We've made it!

309
00:21:43,469 --> 00:21:44,869
A new world!

310
00:21:45,889 --> 00:21:46,549
Finally!

311
00:21:47,029 --> 00:21:48,449
We did it, everybody!

312
00:21:49,809 --> 00:21:51,509
Let's not get ahead of ourselves!

313
00:21:58,509 --> 00:22:00,549
Whoa! They saved us!

314
00:22:00,829 --> 00:22:05,709
Don't worry! As soon as we find Laboon, we'll be sure to let him know where the rest of you are!

315
00:22:07,609 --> 00:22:12,049
It was an honor to meet his family! Please take care, all of you!

316
00:22:12,189 --> 00:22:14,409
Thanks for your help! See you again sometime!

317
00:22:14,409 --> 00:22:22,769
I've heard stories about it, but I never imagined it would be like this!

318
00:22:23,029 --> 00:22:26,529
Turns out the first danger we have to face in the new world...

319
00:22:26,529 --> 00:22:29,369
...is really bad weather!

320
00:22:29,949 --> 00:22:31,469
Oh, look at that lightning!

321
00:22:32,109 --> 00:22:33,549
The winds are raging!

322
00:22:34,089 --> 00:22:35,689
Yeah, the water's rough too!

323
00:22:36,109 --> 00:22:37,529
The needle's going crazy!

324
00:22:37,529 --> 00:22:46,689
I see some ships over there!

325
00:22:46,889 --> 00:22:48,729
Probably pirates having a party!

326
00:22:49,029 --> 00:22:51,429
No way! It's a group of warships!

327
00:22:51,569 --> 00:22:53,169
Sounds like a party to me!

328
00:22:59,529 --> 00:23:01,269
Huh? The Navy?

329
00:23:01,269 --> 00:23:13,949
The Straw Hats surface in the New World at last, but are met with a series of bizarre and dangerous weather conditions.

330
00:23:14,349 --> 00:23:19,869
Soon they encounter a young girl small enough to fit in their hand, and fierce enough to challenge the entire crew.

331
00:23:20,349 --> 00:23:27,309
Tempted by the promise of food, they agree to help her with a rescue operation that sends them hurtling headfirst into a fight with the Navy.

332
00:23:27,309 --> 00:23:33,749
On the next, One Piece! Z's Ambition! Lily the Little Giant! I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

